s^2 &amp; 1 &amp; 100\\
s^1 &amp; -0.2 &amp; 0\\
s^0 &amp; 100 &amp;
\end{array}\] Again, there are two sign changes in the first column. Hence, \(P=2\) Using the Nyquist Stability Criterion, \[N=P-Z=2-2=0\] \[\boxed{0}\]

