\(P(G) = \dfrac{4}{6} = \dfrac{2}{3}\), \(P(R) = \dfrac{2}{6} = \dfrac{1}{3}\), \(n = 7\). Using binomial probability \(P = \binom{7}{k}\left(\dfrac{2}{3}\right)^{k}\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^{7-k}\): <strong>Option (1): \(k=3\) (3 green, 4 red):</strong><br/>\[P = \binom{7}{3}\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{3}\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{4}
    = \frac{35 \times 2^{3}}{3^{7}} = \frac{35 \times 8}{3^{7}} = \frac{280}{3^{7}}\] <strong>Option (2): \(k=4\) (4 green, 3 red):</strong><br/>\[P = \binom{7}{4}\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{4}\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{3}
    = \frac{35 \times 2^{4}}{3^{7}} = \frac{560}{3^{7}}\] <strong>Option (3): \(k=5\) (5 green, 2 red):</strong><br/>\[P = \binom{7}{5}\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{5}\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{2}
    = \frac{21 \times 2^{5}}{3^{7}} = \frac{21 \times 32}{3^{7}} = \frac{672}{3^{7}}\] <strong>Option (4): \(k=6\) (6 green, 1 red):</strong><br/>\[P = \binom{7}{6}\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^{6}\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{1}
    = \frac{7 \times 2^{6}}{3^{7}} = \frac{7 \times 64}{3^{7}} = \frac{448}{3^{7}}\] Comparing: \(\dfrac{672}{3^{7}}\) is maximum (Option 3). \[\boxed{\text{C) Five green faces and two red faces}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>Binomial distribution: \(P(X=k) = \binom{n}{k}p^{k}(1-p)^{n-k}\).</li><li>Most likely outcome \(\approx np = 7 \times \frac{2}{3} \approx 4.67 \Rightarrow k=5\) is nearest integer.</li></ul></div>

Given data: <ul><li>Train speed \(= 54\,\text{km/h}\)</li><li>Time to pass platform \(= 25\,\text{sec}\) (train length + platform length)</li><li>Man speed \(= 9\,\text{km/h}\) (same direction as train)</li><li>Time to pass man \(= 14\,\text{sec}\)</li></ul> <strong>Relative speed of train w.r.t. man:</strong><br/>\[v_{\text{rel}} = 54 - 9 = 45\,\text{km/h} = 45 \times \frac{5}{18} = 12.5\,\text{m/s}\] <strong>Length of train:</strong><br/>\[L_{\text{train}} = v_{\text{rel}} \times t = 14 \times 45 \times \frac{5}{18}
    = 14 \times 12.5 = 175\,\text{m}\] <strong>Length of train + platform:</strong><br/>\[L_{\text{train}} + L_{\text{platform}} = 54 \times \frac{5}{18} \times 25
    = 15 \times 25 = 375\,\text{m}\] <strong>Length of platform:</strong><br/>\[L_{\text{platform}} = 375 - 175 = 200\,\text{m}\] \[\boxed{\text{D) Length of train} = 175\,\text{m},\quad \text{Length of platform} = 200\,\text{m}}\]

Let the common perimeter \(= P\). Then: \[P_{C} = P_{S} = P_{T} \implies \pi D = 4a = 3s\] <strong>Area of circle:</strong><br/>\[A_{C} = \frac{\pi}{4}D^{2} \qquad [\pi D = 4a \Rightarrow D = \tfrac{4a}{\pi}]\] <strong>Area of square:</strong><br/>\[A_{S} = a^{2} = \frac{\pi^{2}D^{2}}{16}\] <strong>Area of equilateral triangle:</strong><br/>\[A_{T} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}s^{2} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}\left(\frac{\pi D}{3}\right)^{2}
    = \frac{\sqrt{3}\,\pi^{2}D^{2}}{36}\] <strong>Comparing coefficients of \(D^{2}\):</strong><br/>\[A_{C} \propto \frac{\pi}{4} \approx 0.785, \quad
    A_{S} \propto \frac{\pi^{2}}{16} \approx 0.617, \quad
    A_{T} \propto \frac{\sqrt{3}\,\pi^{2}}{36} \approx 0.480\] \[\frac{\pi}{4} &gt; \frac{\pi^{2}}{16} &gt; \frac{\sqrt{3}\,\pi^{2}}{36}
    \implies A_{C} &gt; A_{S} &gt; A_{T}\] \[\boxed{\text{A) The circle has the largest area}}\]

Observe the pattern: \(2,\ 12,\ 60,\ 240,\ 720,\ 1440,\ \underline{\hspace{0.8cm}},\ 0\) \[2 \xrightarrow{\times 6} 12 \xrightarrow{\times 5} 60 \xrightarrow{\times 4} 240
    \xrightarrow{\times 3} 720 \xrightarrow{\times 2} 1440 \xrightarrow{\times ?} \underline{\hspace{0.5cm}}
    \xrightarrow{\times 0} 0\] The multipliers are \(6, 5, 4, 3, 2, \ldots\) continuing: next multiplier \(= 2\) (wait — \(720\times2=1440\), then \(1440\times2=2880\), then \(2880\times0=0\)): \[1440 \times 2 = 2880, \qquad 2880 \times 0 = 0\] \[\boxed{\text{A) }2880}\]

